BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:"Public Trust" by Paul Ramírez Jonas: Interactive public artwork
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T173000
UID:6a848355b20478002993b028@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:How serious are the promises we make to one another\, the vows
  we take\, or the pledges made by our civic leaders?\nPaul Ramírez Jonas
 ’s interactive artwork\,\nPublic Trust\n\, asks participants of all ages
  to examine the value of their word by declaring a promise that is recorde
 d in a drawing they can keep.  That promise is then published on a large-s
 cale marquee board and placed alongside commitments made by politicians\, 
 scientists\, economists\, companies\, and weather forecasters\, all drawn 
 daily from headline news.\nIn recognition of International Day of Democrac
 y on September 15\, this interactive art event officially kicks off Toront
 o Public Library's Fall 2026 Celebrate Democracy series. As a vital part o
 f our civic and democratic life\, TPL is proud to host\nPublic Trust\nin c
 ollaboration with\nThe Bentway\n\, an invitation to reflect on community e
 ngagement\, civic participation\, and the promise of democracy as we appro
 ach the municipal election on October 26.\nPlease join us at 6pm for a liv
 e talk with the artist\, Paul Ramírez Jonas\, also hosted at the Fort Yor
 k branch. Visit the\nprogram registration page\nfor more information and t
 o register.\nCheck out the\nKnowYourVote.TO\nwebsite and the\nCelebrate De
 mocracy\npage to learn more about Toronto’s upcoming municipal election\
 , access important voter resources\, and discover activities and interacti
 ve library programs for all ages happening at a branch near you.\nThis eve
 nt is generously supported by the McConnell Foundation.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Branch Atrium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a848355b20478002993b028
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
