BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Adaptive Writing Aid Design Exploration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260829T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260829T150000
UID:6a57e62ce9de6536001becd9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Introduce young children to assistive technology through a fun
 \, hands-on workshop. Using Play-Doh and other safe\, age-appropriate mate
 rials\, kids design and build simple models of assistive devices. While c
 reating\, children develop skills in science\, technology\, engineering\
 , and math by exploring how things work and shaping materials to bring t
 heir ideas to life. The session fosters creativity\, problem-solving\, a
 nd an understanding of inclusion and accessibility.\nInformation Collecti
 on Notice:\nThe Personal Information on this form is collection by the Tor
 onto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c
 )\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program reg
 istration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handl
 es your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl
 .ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.​
LOCATION:Woodside Square\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a57e62ce9de6536001becd9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
