BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rabbit and Bear Paws Puppet Show: The Way
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260926T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260926T150000
UID:6a88a1a3b20478002994833e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:For Children ages 4 to 12 with their parent or caregiver.\nTh
 is interactive puppet show from Chad Solomon features characters from the 
 Rabbit and Bear Paws children's graphic novel series. In this performance\
 , audiences will experience the story of how the turtle carried our world 
 on her back\, and how the tiny muskrat succeeded in giving us the greatest
  gift of all - a place to call home\, Turtle Island.\nChad Solomon\nis a m
 ember of the Henvey Inlet\, First Nation. His grandfather taught him that 
 no matter how old you become\, you should always be young-at-heart and tha
 t laughter is the greatest medicine. This is the spirit behind the comical
  Adventures of Rabbit and Bear Paws series.\nDrop-in only. No Registration
  Required.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a88a1a3b20478002994833e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
